    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what you mean about pareidolia, but it feels way more consistent than just random wind or noise. the spikes on the 17th coincided exactly with when the hum got loudest. if we were talking about something like VLF (very low frequency) or even ELF waves, those are known to penetrate through things and travel long distances, right? is there any theoretical way those atmospheric spikes could act as a carrier for encoded data instead of just being natural interference?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
